  "description": "<p>In:<a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/blob/0696b1830118b6f41091e65553b5589bb252daf4/fcrepo-persistence-ocfl/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/persistence/ocfl/impl/OcflPersistenceConfig.java#L174\" title=\"smart-link\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/blob/0696b1830118b6f41091e65553b5589bb252daf4/fcrepo-persistence-ocfl/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/persistence/ocfl/impl/OcflPersistenceConfig.java#L174</a> </p>\n\n<p><tt>fcrepo.ocfl.s3.timeout.connection.seconds</tt> is currently wired to a netty pool acquisition timeout. Should that instead be wired to a tcp connection timeout? (connectionTimeout in the builder)</p>\n\n\n<p><tt>connectionAcquisitionTimeout(Duration connectionAcquisitionTimeout)</tt></p>\n\n<p>The amount of time to wait when acquiring a connection from the pool before giving up and timing out.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><tt>connectionTimeout(Duration timeout)</tt></p>\n\n<p>The amount of time to wait when initially establishing a connection before giving up and timing out<font color=\"#ffffff\">.</font></p>\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/java/api/latest/software/amazon/awssdk/http/nio/netty/NettyNioAsyncHttpClient.Builder.html\" title=\"smart-link\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://docs.aws.amazon.com/java/api/latest/software/amazon/awssdk/http/nio/netty/NettyNioAsyncHttpClient.Builder.html</a> </p>\n\n\n",
